---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const template = `Dear Council Member [NAME],

I'm writing as a constituent in [DISTRICT/NEIGHBORHOOD] about [CITY]'s contract with Flock Safety for automated license plate reader (ALPR) cameras.

I understand the appeal of tools that help solve crimes. But these systems log every vehicle that passes a camera, not just suspects, and that data can be searched by other agencies, sometimes with little local oversight. [OPTIONAL: cite a specific, sourced example relevant to your area from flockoff.org/database or flockoff.org/legal — don't state a claim you can't back with a link.]

Before this contract is renewed or expanded, I'm asking you to support:

- Public, regular audit logs showing who searches our camera data and why
- Clear limits on which outside agencies, if any, can query our data
- A defined data retention limit
- A real public process, including a council vote, before any renewal or expansion

I'd welcome the chance to discuss this further, or to speak at a future council meeting. Thank you for your time and representation.

Sincerely,
[YOUR NAME]
[YOUR ADDRESS OR NEIGHBORHOOD]
[YOUR EMAIL OR PHONE, OPTIONAL]`;
---

<BaseLayout title="Letter to a Council Member" description="Template letter to a city council member about a Flock Safety ALPR contract.">
  <article class="template-page">
    <p><a href="/act/">← Back to Act in Your City</a></p>
    <h1>Letter to a Council Member</h1>
    <p>
      A short, direct letter tends to get read. Fill in the brackets, and
      cite a specific sourced case from our <a href="/database/">database</a>{" "}
      or <a href="/legal/">legal tracker</a> if one is relevant to your city.
    </p>

    <pre id="letter-template">{template}</pre>
    <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy-target="letter-template">Copy to clipboard</button>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .template-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  pre {
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    background: rgba(232, 232, 232, 0.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(232, 232, 232, 0.15);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1rem;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .copy-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-fg, #e8e8e8);
    color: var(--color-fg, #e8e8e8);
    padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
</style>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".copy-btn").forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const targetId = btn.dataset.copyTarget;
      const el = targetId && document.getElementById(targetId);
      if (!el) return;
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(el.textContent ?? "");
        const original = btn.textContent;
        btn.textContent = "Copied!";
        setTimeout(() => {
          btn.textContent = original;
        }, 1500);
      } catch {
        // clipboard API unavailable/denied - user can still select+copy manually
      }
    });
  });
</script>
